um:</strong> RSI(14) 42.4, up from under 40 last week.</li><li><strong>Ceiling:</strong> the 20-day and 50-day near $185, then the 52-week high $212.94 (Oct 12).</li><li><strong>Floor:</strong> $159.66 (50% of the Jun 25 low $106.37 to the Oct 12 high $212.94), then the Nov 5 low $152.60 and the 200-day $153.57. The 52-week low is $106.37.</li><li><strong>Your tested edge:</strong> the uptrend half applies (price and 50-day above the 200-day). RSI is 42.4, just over your 40 line; it was under 40 when you set this up.</li><li><strong>Plays:</strong> OPEN on the scorecard: PLTR Dec 18 $180 call, entry $757.50 intraday on Nov 11 when price crossed $172.23; marked $745 at the Nov 11 close. Exit rule: a close below $158. Targets $182.77, then $185.5–190.</li><li><strong>Verdict:</strong> the chart supports the upside while closes hold above $172.23, by 17 cents so far. A close below $159.66 would flip it; your own exit at $158 sits just under that. It agrees with management on demand and says nothing yet about bookings.</li></ul>\n<h3 id=\"what-would-change-this-read\">What would change this read</h3>\n<ul><li>Contract value signed and remaining performance obligations in the next report (date not found; early February 2027 estimated).</li><li>Washington: the Dec 11 funding deadline and the defense budget.</li><li>A daily close below $159.66, or above the 50-day near $185.</li></ul>\n<h3 id=\"confidence-and-sources\">Confidence and sources</h3>\n<p>Solid: results and guidance (company release, 10-Q). Thin: the $13.4B and 686 figures appear only in the transcript; insider sales and the valuation multiple come from news write-ups, not filings; no next report date.</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0001321655/000132165526000048/pltr-20260930.htm\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">10-Q</a> · <a href=\"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0001321655/000132165526000045/a2026q3ex991pressrelease.htm\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Press release<